//BUG="a non-void function may fall off the end through a nested branch"
//ERR any

// Every path is covered except one: the outer `else` returns and the inner `if`
// returns, but taking the outer branch without the inner one runs off the end.
// `classify(5)` is that path.
//
// The one the check has to find is buried, so this is what stops a shallow
// implementation that only looks at the last statement of the body, or that
// stops descending once it has seen a `ret` at some level.
//
// 05_functions/27_nested_if_else_returns_on_every_leaf.cpl is the accepted form.

fn classify n
    if n > 0
        if n > 10
            ret 2
    else
        ret 0

fn main
    out "{classify(5)}"
